Z||000000||ur2biteme||03-01-2001||06:18 AM||||well, i got one hell of a deal from a friend, so i really couldnt pass it up.  <P>the fiero has become only semi-reliable at best, so i needed something else.  my best friend has been trying to sell his Z.  i'm getting it for $2500.  now, here's the rundown:<P>All doccumentation of oil changes, repairs, etc. minus the full window sticker (still got the gas mileage paperwork and warranty card) since new.  201k miles with oil changes every 5k.  all options except cruise works.  power windows, a/c, the non-functioning cruise, power mirrors, t-tops, you get the picture.  also, the interior was redone professionally 3 years ago and have been covered ever since.<P>now here's the kicker.  he works for arc audio (does the website, i wish he'd take some of my criticism on it though, lol.) and got paid in equipment to design the site, hence the system it's got. it runs 2 image dynamics 10's, 2 rainbow 6's (you may not have heard of rainbow yet), 2 rainbow tweeters, 2 4's in the stock dash locations, an arc audio 4050 (you may not have heard of arc yet, but you may have heard of zapco.  most of the old zapco guys are now working for, or helped start arc).  it's a 4 channel amp that's pushing about 180w to the subs and powering the 6's and tweeters.  it sounds awesome.  maybe not a competition system, but a VERY clean install and sounds great.  <P>well, when i finally get the down to him, i'll post some pics. i've been looking for the car to drive while i fix stuff on the fiero, and i've found that and WAY more.  this car has to be seen to be appreciated.  i'm no Z nut, but this car may just change my mind.  lol<P>------------------<BR>Bob's '87 econo coupe<BR>aproaching 171k :)<BR> <A HREF="http://members.fortunecity.com/ur2biteme" TARGET=_blank>a little piece of my madness</A>||||reg||1
